---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.CreateAccessAiControlMcpServerRequest
---@field account_id string
---@field id string Unique identifier for the MCP server.
---@field auth_type cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateRequestAuthType|string Authentication method used to connect to the upstream MCP server.
---@field hostname string URL of the upstream MCP endpoint.
---@field name string Display name for the MCP server.
---@field auth_credentials? string Credential configuration for the upstream MCP server. For auth_type "bearer", either a raw token string (e.g. "sk-abc123"), which is wrapped server-side as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, or a JSON-encoded object of the form `{"headers":{"Header-Name":"value",...}}` for custom or multiple static headers (e.g. Cloudflare Access service tokens: `{"headers":{"cf-access-client-id":"...","cf-access-client-secret":"..."}}`). For auth_type "oauth" with a pre-registered client, send a JSON-encoded object containing `auth_mode:"manual"`, `config.authorization_endpoint`, `config.token_endpoint`, and `registration_info.client_id`. Also provide `registration_info.redirect_uris` unless `is_shared_oauth_callback_enabled` is true. Optional fields include `config.issuer`, `config.revocation_endpoint`, `registration_info.scope`, and `registration_info.token_endpoint_auth_method`. Send the client secret in the separate `client_secret` field. Omit `auth_credentials` on update to preserve the existing configuration.
---@field client_secret? string Provides 'client_secret' for a pre-registered OAuth client. This field is accepted on create or update only when 'auth_credentials.auth_mode' is 'manual'. It is required when creating an MCP server with manual OAuth credentials or changing an existing server to use manual OAuth credentials. Omit 'client_secret' on update to preserve the existing secret. Provide a new 'client_secret' to rotate the secret. The secret is never returned by read, create, or update requests.
---@field description? string Optional description of the MCP server.
---@field is_shared_oauth_callback_enabled? boolean When true, per-user authorization uses the shared Cloudflare callback URL as the 'redirect_uri' instead of the portal callback URL. The default is false. Set 'is_shared_oauth_callback_enabled' to true to enable the shared Cloudflare callback URL for this MCP server.
---@field secure_web_gateway? boolean Route outbound traffic to this MCP server through Zero Trust Secure Web Gateway.
---@field updated_prompts? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateRequestUpdatedPromptsList Server-wide prompt capability overrides.
---@field updated_tools? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateRequestUpdatedToolsList Server-wide tool capability overrides.

---Unwrapped `result` payload of the Cloudflare v4 response envelope.
---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.CreateAccessAiControlMcpServerResponse
---@field id string Unique identifier for the MCP server.
---@field auth_type cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateResponseAuthType Authentication method used to connect to the upstream MCP server.
---@field hostname string URL of the upstream MCP endpoint.
---@field name string Display name for the MCP server.
---@field prompts cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateResponsePromptsList
---@field tools cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateResponseToolsList
---@field auth_config_summary? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateResponseAuthConfigSummary|distilled.Null Safe subset of auth_credentials surfaced to the dashboard. Includes auth_mode (dcr|manual), has_client_secret, client_secret_version, and the OAuth endpoints + client_id for manual servers. Never includes the secret value.
---@field authentication_status? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateResponseAuthenticationStatus|distilled.Null Whether administrative authentication is required before capabilities can be synced. Manual OAuth is user-managed and has no administrative authentication flow.
---@field created_at? string|distilled.Null
---@field created_by? string|distilled.Null
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Optional description of the MCP server.
---@field error? string|distilled.Null
---@field error_details? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateResponseErrorDetails|distilled.Null
---@field is_shared_oauth_callback_enabled? boolean|distilled.Null When true, per-user authorization uses the shared Cloudflare callback URL as the 'redirect_uri' instead of the portal callback URL. The default is false. Set 'is_shared_oauth_callback_enabled' to true to enable the shared Cloudflare callback URL for this MCP server.
---@field last_successful_sync? string|distilled.Null
---@field last_synced? string|distilled.Null
---@field modified_at? string|distilled.Null
---@field modified_by? string|distilled.Null
---@field registered_at? string|distilled.Null Timestamp of the most recent successful admin OAuth registration.
---@field secure_web_gateway? boolean|distilled.Null Route outbound traffic to this MCP server through Zero Trust Secure Web Gateway.
---@field status? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateResponseStatus|distilled.Null Current sync state of the server
---@field updated_prompts? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateResponseUpdatedPromptsList|distilled.Null Server-wide prompt capability overrides.
---@field updated_tools? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessAiControlsMcpServersCreateResponseUpdatedToolsList|distilled.Null Server-wide tool capability overrides.

