---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItem
---@field allow_mode_switch? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to allow the user to switch WARP between modes.
---@field allow_updates? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to receive update notifications when a new version of the client is available.
---@field allowed_to_leave? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to allow devices to leave the organization.
---@field auto_connect? number|distilled.Null The amount of time in seconds to reconnect after having been disabled.
---@field browser_extension_config? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemBrowserExtensionConfig|distilled.Null Browser extension proxy settings. Required when profile_type is browser_extension and invalid for WARP profiles.
---@field captive_portal? number|distilled.Null Turn on the captive portal after the specified amount of time.
---@field default? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the policy is the account default. WARP group profiles cannot set this field.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null A description of the policy.
---@field disable_auto_fallback? boolean|distilled.Null If the `dns_server` field of a fallback domain is not present, the client will fall back to a best guess of the default/system DNS resolvers unless this policy option is set to `true`.
---@field dns_search_suffixes? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemDnsSearchSuffixesList|distilled.Null List of DNS search suffixes to apply to clients. Suffixes are evaluated in order. Use an empty array to clear.
---@field enable_device_credential_authentication? boolean|distilled.Null Determines whether the WARP client can silently reauthenticate the user with device credentials (Microsoft Entra) instead of prompting for browser-based reauthentication.
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the policy will be applied to matching devices.
---@field exclude? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemExcludeList|distilled.Null List of routes excluded in the WARP client's tunnel.
---@field exclude_office_ips? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to add Microsoft IPs to Split Tunnel exclusions.
---@field fallback_domains? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemFallbackDomainsList|distilled.Null
---@field gateway_unique_id? string|distilled.Null
---@field global_acceleration? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemGlobalAcceleration|distilled.Null Global Acceleration settings for China. When configured, WARP clients connect to the Global Accelerator addresses instead of the default ones. Please contact your account representative to enable this feature on your account. See https://developers.cloudflare.com/china-network/concepts/global-acceleration/.
---@field include? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemIncludeList|distilled.Null List of routes included in the WARP client's tunnel.
---@field lan_allow_minutes? number|distilled.Null The amount of time in minutes a user is allowed access to their LAN. A value of 0 will allow LAN access until the next WARP reconnection, such as a reboot or a laptop waking from sleep. Note that this field is omitted from the response if null or unset.
---@field lan_allow_subnet_size? number|distilled.Null The size of the subnet for the local access network. Note that this field is omitted from the response if null or unset.
---@field match? string|distilled.Null The wirefilter expression to match devices. Available values: "identity.email", "identity.groups.id", "identity.groups.name", "identity.groups.email", "identity.service_token_uuid", "identity.saml_attributes", "network", "os.name", "os.version", "device.tags".
---@field name? string|distilled.Null The name of the device settings profile.
---@field policy_id? string|distilled.Null
---@field precedence? number|distilled.Null The precedence of the policy. Lower values indicate higher precedence. Policies will be evaluated in ascending order of this field.
---@field profile_type? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemProfileType|distilled.Null The client type to which the device settings profile applies. This field is set when the profile is created and cannot be changed.
---@field register_interface_ip_with_dns? boolean|distilled.Null Determines if the operating system will register WARP's local interface IP with your on-premises DNS server.
---@field sccm_vpn_boundary_support? boolean|distilled.Null Determines whether the WARP client indicates to SCCM that it is inside a VPN boundary. (Windows only).
---@field service_mode_v2? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemServiceModeV2|distilled.Null
---@field support_url? string|distilled.Null The URL to launch when the Send Feedback button is clicked.
---@field switch_locked? boolean|distilled.Null Whether to allow the user to turn off the WARP switch and disconnect the client.
---@field target_tests? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemTargetTestsList|distilled.Null
---@field tunnel_protocol? string|distilled.Null Determines which tunnel protocol to use.
---@field uninstall_protection? boolean|distilled.Null Determines whether uninstalling the WARP client requires an override code. (Windows only).
---@field virtual_networks? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemVirtualNetworks|distilled.Null Virtual network access settings for the device.

---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemBrowserExtensionConfig
---@field proxy_control cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemBrowserExtensionConfigProxyControl Whether the user may disable the browser extension proxy.
---@field proxy_enabled boolean Whether the browser extension proxy is active.

---@alias cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomListResultItemBrowserExtensionConfigProxyControl "unlocked"|"locked"

