---@alias cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseAction "on"|"off"|"allow"|"block"|"scan"|"noscan"|"safesearch"|"ytrestricted"|"isolate"|"noisolate"|"override"|"l4_override"|"egress"|"resolve"|"quarantine"|"redirect"|"forward"

---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseExpiration
---@field expires_at string Show the timestamp when the policy expires and stops applying. The value must follow RFC 3339 and include a UTC offset. The system accepts non-zero offsets but converts them to the equivalent UTC+00:00 value and returns timestamps with a trailing Z. Expiration policies ignore client timezones and expire globally at the specified expires_at time.
---@field duration? number|distilled.Null Defines the default duration a policy active in minutes. Must set in order to use the `reset_expiration` endpoint on this rule.
---@field expired? boolean|distilled.Null Indicates whether the policy is expired.

---@alias cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseFiltersItem "http"|"dns"|"l4"|"egress"|"dns_resolver"

---@alias cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseFiltersList cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseFiltersItem[]

---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettings
---@field add_headers? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsAddHeadersMap|distilled.Null Add custom headers to allowed requests as key-value pairs. Use header names as keys that map to arrays of header values. Header values may contain `@{selector.name}` variable references that are interpolated at the edge. Use `@@{` to escape a literal `@{`. A maximum of 20 header operations (add + set + delete) is allowed per policy. Each header name may not exceed 256 bytes and each header value may not exceed 4 KB. Settable only for `http` rules with the action set to `allow`.
---@field allow_child_bypass? boolean|distilled.Null Set to enable MSP children to bypass this rule. Only parent MSP accounts can set this. this rule. Settable for all types of rules.
---@field biso_admin_controls? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsBisoAdminControls|distilled.Null Configure browser isolation behavior. Settable only for `http` rules with the action set to `isolate`.
---@field block_page? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsBlockPage|distilled.Null Configure custom block page settings. If missing or null, use the account settings. Settable only for `http` rules with the action set to `block`.
---@field block_page_enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Enable the custom block page. Settable only for `dns` rules with action `block`.
---@field block_reason? string|distilled.Null Explain why the rule blocks the request. The custom block page shows this text (if enabled). Settable only for `dns`, `l4`, and `http` rules when the action set to `block`.
---@field bypass_parent_rule? boolean|distilled.Null Set to enable MSP accounts to bypass their parent's rules. Only MSP child accounts can set this. Settable for all types of rules.
---@field check_session? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsCheckSession|distilled.Null Configure session check behavior. Settable only for `l4` and `http` rules with the action set to `allow`.
---@field delete_headers? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsDeleteHeadersList|distilled.Null Remove headers from allowed requests by name. A maximum of 20 header operations (add + set + delete) is allowed per policy. Each header name may not exceed 256 bytes. Settable only for `http` rules with the action set to `allow`.
---@field dns_resolvers? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsDnsResolvers|distilled.Null Configure custom resolvers to route queries that match the resolver policy. Unused with 'resolve_dns_through_cloudflare' or 'resolve_dns_internally' settings. DNS queries get routed to the address closest to their origin. Only valid when a rule's action set to 'resolve'. Settable only for `dns_resolver` rules.
---@field egress? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsEgress|distilled.Null Configure how Gateway Proxy traffic egresses. You can enable this setting for rules with Egress actions and filters, or omit it to indicate local egress via WARP IPs. Settable only for `egress` rules.
---@field forensic_copy? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsForensicCopy|distilled.Null Configure whether a copy of the HTTP request will be sent to storage when the rule matches.
---@field forward? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsForward|distilled.Null Forward matching HTTP requests to a Worker. Required for `http` rules with the action set to `forward`.
---@field ignore_cname_category_matches? boolean|distilled.Null Ignore category matches at CNAME domains in a response. When off, evaluate categories in this rule against all CNAME domain categories in the response. Settable only for `dns` and `dns_resolver` rules.
---@field insecure_disable_dnssec_validation? boolean|distilled.Null Specify whether to disable DNSSEC validation (for Allow actions) [INSECURE]. Settable only for `dns` rules.
---@field ip_categories? boolean|distilled.Null Enable IPs in DNS resolver category blocks. The system blocks only domain name categories unless you enable this setting. Settable only for `dns` and `dns_resolver` rules.
---@field ip_indicator_feeds? boolean|distilled.Null Indicates whether to include IPs in DNS resolver indicator feed blocks. Default, indicator feeds block only domain names. Settable only for `dns` and `dns_resolver` rules.
---@field l4override? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsL4override|distilled.Null Send matching traffic to the supplied destination IP address and port. Settable only for `l4` rules with the action set to `l4_override`.
---@field notification_settings? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsNotificationSettings|distilled.Null Configure a notification to display on the user's device when this rule matched. Settable for all types of rules with the action set to `block`.
---@field override_host? string|distilled.Null Defines a hostname for override, for the matching DNS queries. Settable only for `dns` rules with the action set to `override`.
---@field override_ips? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsOverrideIpsList|distilled.Null Defines a an IP or set of IPs for overriding matched DNS queries. Settable only for `dns` rules with the action set to `override`.
---@field payload_log? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsPayloadLog|distilled.Null Configure DLP payload logging. Settable only for `http` rules.
---@field quarantine? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsQuarantine|distilled.Null Configure settings that apply to quarantine rules. Settable only for `http` rules.
---@field redirect? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsRedirect|distilled.Null Apply settings to redirect rules. Settable only for `http` rules with the action set to `redirect`.
---@field resolve_dns_internally? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsResolveDnsInternally|distilled.Null Configure to forward the query to the internal DNS service, passing the specified 'view_id' as input. Not used when 'dns_resolvers' is specified or 'resolve_dns_through_cloudflare' is set. Only valid when a rule's action set to 'resolve'. Settable only for `dns_resolver` rules.
---@field resolve_dns_through_cloudflare? boolean|distilled.Null Enable to send queries that match the policy to Cloudflare's default 1.1.1.1 DNS resolver. Cannot set when 'dns_resolvers' specified or 'resolve_dns_internally' is set. Only valid when a rule's action set to 'resolve'. Settable only for `dns_resolver` rules.
---@field set_headers? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsSetHeadersMap|distilled.Null Replace existing headers on allowed requests with the specified key-value pairs. If a header does not exist, it is added. Header values may contain `@{selector.name}` variable references that are interpolated at the edge. Use `@@{` to escape a literal `@{`. A maximum of 20 header operations (add + set + delete) is allowed per policy. Each header name may not exceed 256 bytes and each header value may not exceed 4 KB. Settable only for `http` rules with the action set to `allow`.
---@field untrusted_cert? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettingsUntrustedCert|distilled.Null Configure behavior when an upstream certificate is invalid or an SSL error occurs. Settable only for `http` rules with the action set to `allow`.

