---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.IdentityProvidersCreateRequestScimConfig
---@field enabled? boolean A flag to enable or disable SCIM for the identity provider.
---@field identity_update_behavior? cloudflare.zero_trust.IdentityProvidersCreateRequestScimConfigIdentityUpdateBehavior|string Indicates how a SCIM event updates a user identity used for policy evaluation. Use "automatic" to automatically update a user's identity and augment it with fields from the SCIM user resource. Use "reauth" to force re-authentication on group membership updates, user identity update will only occur after successful re-authentication. With "reauth" identities will not contain fields from the SCIM user resource. With "no_action" identities will not be changed by SCIM updates in any way and users will not be prompted to reauthenticate.
---@field scim_base_url? string The base URL of Cloudflare's SCIM V2.0 API endpoint.
---@field seat_deprovision? boolean A flag to remove a user's seat in Zero Trust when they have been deprovisioned in the Identity Provider. This cannot be enabled unless user_deprovision is also enabled.
---@field secret? string A read-only token generated when the SCIM integration is enabled for the first time. It is redacted on subsequent requests. If you lose this you will need to refresh it at /access/identity_providers/:idpID/refresh_scim_secret.
---@field user_deprovision? boolean A flag to enable revoking a user's session in Access and Gateway when they have been deprovisioned in the Identity Provider.

---@alias cloudflare.zero_trust.IdentityProvidersCreateRequestScimConfigIdentityUpdateBehavior "automatic"|"reauth"|"no_action"

