---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.ListResourceLibraryApplicationsRequest
---@field account_id string
---@field cursor? string Opaque value from `result_info.cursor` of the previous response. Returns the results that follow it. Send the same `filter`, `search`, `lookup`, and `order_by` values as the request that returned it; `limit` and `fields` may change. An empty value is the same as no cursor. A modified cursor, or one used with different values, returns `400`.
---@field fields? string Return only the listed properties on each application, as a comma-separated list. Use this to keep responses small when you only need part of each application, for example populating a picker with `fields=id,name` instead of downloading every hostname and IP subnet.
---@field filter? string Filter applications using `key:value` format. Supported filter keys:
---@field limit? number Number of results to return. Defaults to 25; values are clamped to 1–250.
---@field lookup? string Find complete, case-insensitive application name mentions in a phrase or rule sentence. Misspelled names do not match. Returns matching applications ranked by relevance. Must be between 2 and 1000 characters, with no control characters other than tab and line breaks. Uses the same filters, fields, and pagination as listing. `search` cannot be combined with lookup. Results are ranked by relevance, so `order_by` is ignored. To keep the text out of URLs, send it to `POST .../applications/lookup` instead.
---@field offset? number Number of results to skip. Defaults to 0; negative values are clamped to 0. Ignored when `cursor` is provided.
---@field order_by? string Order results using field:direction format. Supported fields are name, id, human_id, category_id, application_type, application_confidence_score, and gen_ai_score. Supported directions are asc and desc. name and application_type ignore the case of the letters A to Z, and ties sort by id. Ignored when search is provided; results are ranked by relevance instead. Also ignored when lookup is provided.
---@field search? string Fuzzy search across application name and hostnames. Results are ranked by relevance. Must be between 2 and 200 characters. Can be combined with filter parameters.

