---@field default? boolean Whether the policy is the account default. WARP group profiles cannot set this field.
---@field description? string A description of the policy.
---@field disable_auto_fallback? boolean If the `dns_server` field of a fallback domain is not present, the client will fall back to a best guess of the default/system DNS resolvers unless this policy option is set to `true`.
---@field dns_search_suffixes? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomEditRequestDnsSearchSuffixesList List of DNS search suffixes to apply to clients. Suffixes are evaluated in order. Use an empty array to clear.
---@field enable_device_credential_authentication? boolean Determines whether the WARP client can silently reauthenticate the user with device credentials (Microsoft Entra) instead of prompting for browser-based reauthentication.
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the policy will be applied to matching devices.
---@field exclude? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomEditRequestExcludeList List of routes excluded in the WARP client's tunnel. Both 'exclude' and 'include' cannot be set in the same request.
---@field exclude_office_ips? boolean Whether to add Microsoft IPs to Split Tunnel exclusions.
---@field global_acceleration? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomEditRequestGlobalAcceleration Global Acceleration settings for China. When configured, WARP clients connect to the Global Accelerator addresses instead of the default ones. Please contact your account representative to enable this feature on your account. See https://developers.cloudflare.com/china-network/concepts/global-acceleration/.
---@field include? cloudflare.zero_trust.DevicesPoliciesCustomEditRequestIncludeList List of routes included in the WARP client's tunnel. Both 'exclude' and 'include' cannot be set in the same request.
