---Unwrapped `result` payload of the Cloudflare v4 response envelope.
---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.RefreshAccessServiceTokenResponse
---@field id? string|distilled.Null The ID of the service token.
---@field client_id? string|distilled.Null The Client ID for the service token. Access will check for this value in the `CF-Access-Client-ID` request header.
---@field duration? string|distilled.Null The duration for how long the service token will be valid. Must be in the format `300ms` or `2h45m`, or the special value `forever` for non-expiring tokens. Valid time units are: ns, us (or µs), ms, s, m, h. The default is 1 year in hours (8760h).
---@field enabled? boolean|distilled.Null Whether the service token is enabled. A disabled service token cannot be used to authenticate; both its current and previous `client_secret` stop being accepted, but the token itself is preserved and can be re-enabled. A service token reported as leaked is disabled automatically and cannot be re-enabled until its secret is rotated; attempting to do so returns a 409. Defaults to enabled when omitted on create.
---@field expires_at? string|distilled.Null
---@field leak_report_url? string|distilled.Null Where the leaked `client_secret` was found, if provided by the reporter. Omitted if the token has not been reported as leaked.
---@field leak_reported_at? string|distilled.Null When a secret scanning partner reported this service token's `client_secret` as leaked. A leaked service token is disabled and must be rotated before it can be re-enabled. Cleared once the secret is rotated. Omitted if the token has not been reported as leaked.
---@field leak_reporter? string|distilled.Null The secret scanning partner that reported the leak. Omitted if the token has not been reported as leaked.
---@field name? string|distilled.Null The name of the service token.
---@field tags? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessServiceTokensRefreshResponseTagsMap|distilled.Null Tags associated with the service token, as key-value pairs. On update, replaces all existing tags.

