---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.ResetExpirationGatewayRuleResponse
---@field action cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseAction Specify the action to perform when the associated traffic, identity, and device posture expressions either absent or evaluate to `true`.
---@field enabled boolean Specify whether the rule is enabled.
---@field filters cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseFiltersList Specify the protocol or layer to evaluate the traffic, identity, and device posture expressions. Can only contain a single value.
---@field name string Specify the rule name.
---@field precedence number Set the order of your rules. Lower values indicate higher precedence. At each processing phase, evaluate applicable rules in ascending order of this value. Refer to [Order of enforcement](http://developers.cloudflare.com/learning-paths/secure-internet-traffic/understand-policies/order-of-enforcement/#manage-precedence-with-terraform) to manage precedence via Terraform.
---@field traffic string Specify the wirefilter expression used for traffic matching. The API automatically formats and sanitizes expressions before storing them. To prevent Terraform state drift, use the formatted expression returned in the API response.
---@field id? string|distilled.Null Identify the API resource with a UUID.
---@field created_at? string|distilled.Null
---@field deleted_at? string|distilled.Null Indicate the date of deletion, if any.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Specify the rule description.
---@field device_posture? string|distilled.Null Specify the wirefilter expression used for device posture check. The API automatically formats and sanitizes expressions before storing them. To prevent Terraform state drift, use the formatted expression returned in the API response.
---@field expiration? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseExpiration|distilled.Null Defines the expiration time stamp and default duration of a DNS policy. Takes precedence over the policy's `schedule` configuration, if any. This does not apply to HTTP or network policies. Settable only for `dns` rules.
---@field identity? string|distilled.Null Specify the wirefilter expression used for identity matching. The API automatically formats and sanitizes expressions before storing them. To prevent Terraform state drift, use the formatted expression returned in the API response.
---@field read_only? boolean|distilled.Null Indicate that this rule is shared via the Orgs API and read only.
---@field rule_settings? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseRuleSettings|distilled.Null Defines settings for this rule. Settings apply only to specific rule types and must use compatible selectors. If Terraform detects drift, confirm the setting supports your rule type and check whether the API modifies the value. Use API-returned values in your configuration to prevent drift.
---@field schedule? cloudflare.zero_trust.GatewayRulesResetExpirationResponseSchedule|distilled.Null Defines the schedule for activating DNS policies. Settable only for `dns` and `dns_resolver` rules.
---@field sharable? boolean|distilled.Null Indicate that this rule is sharable via the Orgs API.
---@field source_account? string|distilled.Null Provide the account tag of the account that created the rule.
---@field updated_at? string|distilled.Null
---@field version? number|distilled.Null Indicate the version number of the rule(read-only).
---@field warning_status? string|distilled.Null Indicate a warning for a misconfigured rule, if any.

