---@class cloudflare.zero_trust.UpdateAccessServiceTokenForAccountRequest
---@field account_id string The Account ID to use for this endpoint. Mutually exclusive with the Zone ID.
---@field service_token_id string UUID.
---@field client_secret_version? number A version number identifying the current `client_secret` associated with the service token. Incrementing it triggers a rotation; the previous secret will still be accepted until the time indicated by `previous_client_secret_expires_at`. If the service token was reported as leaked, `previous_client_secret_expires_at` is not required, may not be in the future, and the previous secret is discarded immediately.
---@field duration? string The duration for how long the service token will be valid. Must be in the format `300ms` or `2h45m`, or the special value `forever` for non-expiring tokens. Valid time units are: ns, us (or µs), ms, s, m, h. The default is 1 year in hours (8760h).
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the service token is enabled. A disabled service token cannot be used to authenticate; both its current and previous `client_secret` stop being accepted, but the token itself is preserved and can be re-enabled. A service token reported as leaked is disabled automatically and cannot be re-enabled until its secret is rotated; attempting to do so returns a 409. Defaults to enabled when omitted on create.
---@field name? string The name of the service token.
---@field previous_client_secret_expires_at? string The expiration of the previous `client_secret`. This can be modified at any point after a rotation. For example, you may extend it further into the future if you need more time to update services with the new secret; or move it into the past to immediately invalidate the previous token in case of compromise. Rotating a service token that was reported as leaked discards the previous secret entirely, so no grace period can be set.
---@field tags? cloudflare.zero_trust.AccessServiceTokensUpdateRequestTagsMap Tags associated with the service token, as key-value pairs. On update, replaces all existing tags.

