---Check a candidate custom finding type without creating it, so problems can be corrected before publishing. The request body is the same shape as `CreateFindingType`, and the candidate is checked against the same rules, so a valid result means the definition itself is sound. It is not a reservation: a create can still be rejected for a reason that does not belong to the definition, such as the account already holding the maximum number of custom finding types. A candidate that fails validation is still a **200** with `result.valid: false` and one entry in `result.errors` per problem — that is the answer this endpoint exists to give. `4xx` is reserved for a request that could not be processed at all, such as a body that will not parse.
---
---`POST /accounts/{account_id}/data-security/posture/finding_types/validate`
---@param input cloudflare.zero_trust.ValidateCasbPostureFindingTypeRequest
---@return cloudflare.zero_trust.ValidateCasbPostureFindingTypeResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:validate_casb_posture_finding_type(input) end

---Validates whether this pattern is a valid regular expression. Rejects it if the regular expression is too complex or can match an unbounded-length string. The regex will be rejected if it uses `*` or `+`. Bound the maximum number of characters that can be matched using a range, e.g. `{1,100}`.
---
---`POST /accounts/{account_id}/dlp/patterns/validate`
---@param input cloudflare.zero_trust.ValidateDlpPatternRequest
